eep it. When the picks held every model listed then, one the vendor lists since is served first beside them (`withNewlyListed`, `Picks`); one listed then and left unpicked stays out. A remote magpie's routing group listed since is served beside any picks, ones that left models out too, so a group made there shows in the agents' pickers with no tick (KoiLx0 on X, `TestRemoteMagpieNewGroupServedBesidePicks`); one listed at Save and left unpicked stays out. Picks saved before `PickedFrom` was kept are taken to hold every model when they hold every one released up to the newest of them (models.dev's `release_date`), so a Claude account whose user picked them all is served Haiku 5.5 (wakaka). The editor and the TUI start from `Picks`, so a later Save keeps the new model. While some picks are set aside (the list is known to be short), a save with new picks keeps the models the earlier `PickedFrom` had beside those listed now, so a model the user saw and left unpicked isn't new when that list has it again; a list short of no pick is taken as it is. A pick a list fetched again stops listing (`Refetch`, `KeepListsFresh`, and a plugin's hourly `KeepPluginsListed`) leaves `Models` for `Delisted` (`dropGonePicks`), not served, and goes back among the picks when a later list has it (`relistPicks`): Our Free Model's plugin lists its account channels' models only once its service has read them after a restart, and its free pools only while they answer, so each magpie update had its user pick every model again (多喝热水 on Discord). Every save keeps `Delisted` but for what it picks again (`delistedWith`); Select none clears it. A provider whose every pick is in `Delisted` serves none of its models for `pickWait` (an hour) from when the last one left (`DelistedAt`, `waitsForPicks`), not the vendor's list; after that, or for picks set aside before `DelistedAt` was kept, the picks are taken as gone for good and the list is served as if none were picked, while they still come back with a list that has them. WorkBuddy AI took its Free plan's deepseek-v4.1-flash off its list for hy3, and an account whose one pick it was got no model in the agents' picker, its row reading "1 image model" (maxleebeta on Discord). `KeepPluginsListed` asks again after `relistSoon` (5 minutes) when a list left a pick out. Devin's picks and set-aside picks are read without Adaptive and Fusion, in any case (`withoutDevinRouters` in `normalize`): the built-in listed them before it served Devin's chat API (ce8d0e065), which answers either with 502 "no API providers are available", and picks saved then were served as the user's own models after the move to the plugin, which lists neither (`TestDevinRouterPicksNotServed`). `TestPluginPicksComeBackWithTheirList`, `TestEveryPickDelistedServesNone`, `TestPicksGoneForGoodServeTheList` and `TestRelayPicksComeBackWithTheirList` cover it. | [`models.go`](../../internal/provider/models.go), [`provider.go`](../../internal/provider/provider.go) |
